# Extra exam questions, part D: core business-administration areas that carry weight on the
# 2026-27 Finance district blueprint (EI 9, PD 13, COM 5, CR 5, OP 6, EC 6, NF 6, EN 1, HR 1, MK 1, SM 1).
# Format: (PI, stem, [correct answer FIRST, then 3 wrong answers], explanation). The app shuffles options.
# All original questions written for this app. Not copied from DECA or MBA Research.
Q = []
def q(pi, stem, opts, exp): Q.append((pi, stem, opts, exp))

# ---------------- Emotional Intelligence ----------------
q("EI:001","Recognizing that you are getting frustrated during a tense client meeting and calming yourself before you respond shows which part of emotional intelligence?",
  ["Self-regulation","Social awareness","Motivation","Technical skill"],
  "Self-regulation means managing your own emotions and impulses once you notice them. Social awareness is reading other people's emotions.")
q("EI:001","Which statement best describes emotional intelligence?",
  ["The ability to recognize and manage your own emotions and the emotions of others","A score that measures how quickly a person learns new information","The ability to hide emotions completely while at work","A personality type that stays the same throughout life"],
  "EI is about understanding and managing emotions, yours and other people's. Unlike IQ, it can be developed with practice.")
q("EI:030","A client tells a financial advisor she is scared because her husband just lost his job. Which response shows empathy?",
  ["\"That sounds really stressful. Let's look at what we can do to keep your family steady.\"","\"Job losses happen all the time. You'll be fine.\"","\"Let's not talk about that and focus on your portfolio.\"","\"You should have built a bigger emergency fund.\""],
  "Empathy means acknowledging the other person's feelings and showing you understand before moving to solutions.")
q("EI:103","A bank teller sees that a well-known local businessman has a very low account balance. What should the teller do with this information?",
  ["Keep it confidential and use it only for the transaction","Tell coworkers so they are careful with his checks","Mention it to his business partner","Post a general warning without naming him"],
  "Finance employees must keep customer information confidential. Sharing it with anyone who doesn't need it for the job is unethical and can break privacy laws.")
q("EI:022","Mateo realizes he gave a client the wrong interest rate on a loan quote. What should he do to demonstrate integrity?",
  ["Contact the client right away, admit the error and give the correct rate","Wait to see if the client notices","Blame the rate sheet he was given","Honor the wrong rate secretly and hide the difference"],
  "Integrity means being honest even when it is uncomfortable. Owning the mistake quickly protects the client's trust.")
q("EI:024","An analyst notices that a monthly report takes four hours to build by hand. Without being asked, she creates a spreadsheet template that cuts it to 30 minutes. She is showing",
  ["initiative.","assertiveness.","tolerance for ambiguity.","self-control."],
  "Initiative is taking action to improve things without waiting to be told.")
q("EI:025","A customer yells at a loan officer because his application was denied. The loan officer keeps a calm voice and does not raise her own. She is demonstrating",
  ["self-control.","aggressiveness.","passive behavior.","office politics."],
  "Self-control is managing your reactions, especially under pressure, so emotions don't drive your behavior.")
q("EI:003","Which is the best way to use feedback for personal growth?",
  ["Listen without getting defensive, ask clarifying questions and make a plan to improve","Ask for feedback only from people who agree with you","Explain why the feedback is wrong","Ignore feedback that isn't written down"],
  "Feedback helps only if you take it in openly, understand it and act on it.")
q("EI:026","A bank switches to a new loan software system. Which employee is adjusting to change best?",
  ["Dana, who attends the training and asks how the new system can help her clients","Eli, who keeps using paper forms until he is forced to switch","Fran, who complains the old system was fine","Gus, who asks to transfer to another branch"],
  "Adjusting to change means accepting it, learning what is needed and looking for its benefits.")
q("EI:015","Two coworkers disagree over who should present to a client. Their manager has each explain their view and then helps them find a plan they both accept. Which conflict-resolution approach is this?",
  ["Collaborating","Avoiding","Forcing","Accommodating"],
  "Collaborating looks for a win-win solution that meets both people's needs. Avoiding ignores the conflict; forcing imposes one side.")
q("EI:062","In a negotiation, the point at which you will walk away rather than accept a worse deal is your",
  ["bottom line (resistance point).","opening offer.","concession.","agenda."],
  "Knowing your bottom line before you start keeps you from agreeing to a deal that is worse than having no deal.")
q("EI:011","A team discusses options until every member can support the final decision, even if it wasn't everyone's first choice. This is",
  ["consensus building.","majority voting.","groupthink.","delegation."],
  "Consensus means everyone can accept and support the decision. Groupthink is when people go along without raising real concerns.")
q("EI:009","A department manager gets employees to work toward a shared goal by inspiring them rather than relying only on her job title. She is showing",
  ["leadership.","micromanagement.","authority without influence.","office politics."],
  "Leadership is the ability to influence and inspire others toward goals. Authority comes from a position; leadership can come from anyone.")
q("EI:131","Which action best shows ethical leadership by a branch manager?",
  ["Following the same rules she expects employees to follow","Setting sales goals so high that employees cut corners","Rewarding results no matter how they were achieved","Keeping bad news from the regional office"],
  "Ethical leaders model the behavior they expect and create a culture where doing the right thing is rewarded.")
q("EI:017","A loan officer assumes an older applicant won't understand the bank's mobile app and doesn't mention it. This is an example of",
  ["a personal bias or stereotype.","good customer service.","tolerance for ambiguity.","an internal control."],
  "Making assumptions about someone based on a group they belong to is stereotyping. Professionals should recognize and set aside these biases.")
q("EI:033","A financial advisor learns that a client's culture places a high value on family decision-making, so she invites the client's adult children to the planning meeting at the client's request. She is showing",
  ["cultural sensitivity.","favoritism.","a conflict of interest.","assertiveness."],
  "Cultural sensitivity means being aware of and respecting cultural differences and adapting your approach.")
q("EI:028","Which is a healthy way to manage stress during a busy tax season?",
  ["Breaking big tasks into smaller steps and taking short breaks","Skipping sleep to work more hours every night","Keeping all frustrations to yourself","Taking on extra projects to stay distracted"],
  "Good stress management includes planning, prioritizing, rest and short breaks. Skipping sleep makes stress and mistakes worse.")
q("EI:077","An employee promises a client a report by Friday but realizes on Wednesday it will be late. The best way to manage this commitment is to",
  ["tell the client now and give a realistic new date","turn in an unfinished report on Friday","say nothing and deliver it Monday","ask a coworker to make an excuse"],
  "Managing commitments means meeting deadlines or communicating early and honestly when you can't.")
q("EI:036","Which behavior best shows treating others with dignity and respect?",
  ["Listening to a coworker's idea fully before responding","Correcting a coworker's mistake in front of a client","Interrupting to save time","Using a nickname a coworker has asked you not to use"],
  "Respect includes listening, valuing others' input and addressing problems privately and politely.")
q("EI:005","A manager who explains why a change is needed, involves employees in planning it and celebrates early wins is",
  ["leading change effectively.","using power inappropriately.","avoiding conflict.","practicing office politics."],
  "Leading change means communicating the reason, involving people and reinforcing progress.")
q("EI:064","The shared values, beliefs and behaviors that shape how employees work together in a company are its",
  ["organizational culture.","chain of command.","mission statement.","bylaws."],
  "Organizational culture is \"the way we do things here.\" A mission statement is a written statement of purpose.")
q("EI:104","A team leader assigns the detail-oriented, analytical employee to check the numbers and the outgoing, people-oriented employee to present to the client. She is",
  ["leveraging personality types.","showing favoritism.","avoiding responsibility.","stereotyping."],
  "Matching tasks to people's personality strengths helps a team perform better.")
q("EI:014","Which is the most effective way to recognize an employee's contribution?",
  ["Give specific, timely praise that names what the employee did well","Wait until the annual review to mention it","Praise the whole department in general terms","Give a reward only when the employee asks"],
  "Recognition works best when it is specific, sincere and given soon after the behavior.")

# ---------------- Professional Development ----------------
q("PD:017","What is the first step in the decision-making process?",
  ["Define the problem or decision to be made","Choose the best alternative","Evaluate the results","List possible solutions"],
  "You can't solve a problem until you clearly define it. The usual steps: define, gather information, list alternatives, evaluate, choose, act, review.")
q("PD:077","A bank's online loan applications drop 30%. Before suggesting solutions, the team reviews website data and talks to customers. They are",
  ["gathering information to identify the cause of the problem.","implementing a solution.","evaluating the results.","brainstorming alternatives."],
  "Good problem solving finds the root cause first, using data, before choosing a solution.")
q("PD:019","Which is the best example of time management?",
  ["Ranking tasks by importance and due date, then doing the most important first","Checking email every five minutes","Doing the easiest tasks first to feel productive","Saying yes to every request"],
  "Prioritizing by urgency and importance keeps you working on what matters most.")
q("PD:009","An accountant follows the same checklist every month to close the books so nothing is missed. She is demonstrating",
  ["systematic behavior.","creativity.","initiative.","tolerance for ambiguity."],
  "Systematic behavior means working in an organized, step-by-step way.")
q("PD:002","Why does personal appearance matter for a financial advisor meeting a new client?",
  ["Clients form first impressions quickly, and a professional look builds trust","It is required by federal law","It replaces the need for product knowledge","It allows the advisor to charge higher fees"],
  "In finance, clients are trusting you with their money. A professional appearance supports a credible first impression.")
q("PD:021","Which law sets the federal minimum wage and overtime pay rules for most U.S. workers?",
  ["Fair Labor Standards Act","Sarbanes-Oxley Act","Dodd-Frank Act","Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act"],
  "The Fair Labor Standards Act (1938) covers minimum wage, overtime and child labor. The others are finance laws.")
q("PD:028","During a job interview for a bank analyst position, which response best answers \"Tell me about a time you made a mistake\"?",
  ["Describe a real mistake, what you did to fix it and what you learned","Say you have never made a mistake","Blame a former coworker","Change the subject to your strengths"],
  "Interviewers want honesty, accountability and evidence that you learn. A short story with the fix and the lesson works best.")
q("PD:031","Which belongs on a resume for a high school student applying for a bank internship?",
  ["DECA competition results and a part-time job with responsibilities and results","A photo and Social Security number","A list of every class taken since ninth grade","Salary expectations"],
  "A resume should show relevant experience, skills and achievements. Never include a Social Security number.")
q("PD:029","When should you send a thank-you or follow-up message after a job interview?",
  ["Within 24 hours","Only if you don't hear back in a month","Only if you got the job","Before the interview"],
  "A prompt follow-up within a day shows professionalism and keeps you top of mind.")
q("PD:037","Which is the best example of networking to find a finance job?",
  ["Asking a family friend who is a CPA for an informational interview","Applying to 100 job postings without researching them","Waiting for employers to contact you","Posting complaints about your current job online"],
  "Networking means building relationships with people who can share advice and job leads. Informational interviews are a classic tool.")
q("PD:032","A student who wants to work in banking volunteers to help with a free tax-preparation program at a community center. She is",
  ["gaining work experience through volunteering.","building a professional certification.","practicing office politics.","completing a job application."],
  "Volunteering, internships and job shadowing are ways to gain experience before your first full-time job.")
q("PD:033","Why is ongoing education important for finance professionals?",
  ["Laws, technology and products change, so skills must be updated","It guarantees a promotion every year","It is only needed for people who change careers","It replaces on-the-job experience"],
  "Many finance credentials (CFP, CPA, FINRA licenses) require continuing education because regulations and products change.")
q("PD:126","A bank creates a feature that rounds up every debit card purchase and moves the spare change into savings. This is an example of",
  ["innovation.","consolidation.","compliance.","a sunk cost."],
  "Innovation is turning a new idea into a product, service or process that creates value.")
q("PD:018","Which is a SMART goal?",
  ["Save $1,200 for an emergency fund by June 30 by depositing $100 a month","Save more money","Become rich someday","Spend less on things I don't need"],
  "SMART goals are Specific, Measurable, Achievable, Relevant and Time-bound.")
q("PD:152","Which job involves reviewing loan applications and deciding whether borrowers meet the lender's standards?",
  ["Loan underwriter","Actuary","Compliance officer","Auditor"],
  "Underwriters evaluate risk to decide whether to approve loans or insurance. Actuaries calculate risk using statistics.")
q("PD:152","Which professional uses statistics and math to calculate the probability and cost of future events for insurance companies?",
  ["Actuary","Teller","Underwriter","Financial planner"],
  "Actuaries analyze data to price insurance policies and estimate future claims.")
q("PD:152","Which credential is most closely associated with personal financial planning?",
  ["Certified Financial Planner (CFP)","Certified Public Accountant (CPA)","Chartered Financial Analyst (CFA)","Certified Internal Auditor (CIA)"],
  "The CFP is the best-known planning credential. CPAs specialize in accounting and tax; CFAs in investment analysis.")
q("PD:153","A new financial advisor joins the local chamber of commerce and attends its monthly events. The main purpose is to",
  ["build relationships that can lead to referrals and clients","avoid having to make sales calls","meet continuing education requirements","get free advertising"],
  "Professional associations and community groups are common ways to build a network in finance.")
q("PD:213","A company with strong corporate governance is most likely to",
  ["attract investors and borrow money at a lower cost","avoid all government regulation","pay no taxes","never have a lawsuit"],
  "Investors and lenders see well-governed companies as lower-risk, which lowers the cost of capital.")
q("PD:214","Which committee of the board of directors oversees the company's financial reporting and works with the external auditors?",
  ["Audit committee","Marketing committee","Compensation committee","Social committee"],
  "The audit committee, made up of independent directors, oversees financial reporting, internal controls and auditors.")
q("PD:214","Having the CEO and the board chair be two different people is meant to",
  ["give the board independent oversight of management","save money on salaries","make decisions faster","give the CEO more power"],
  "Separating the roles helps the board hold management accountable.")
q("PD:301","An employee who reports a suspected accounting violation through the company's ethics hotline is helping to",
  ["achieve the company's governance objectives.","undermine the board of directors.","violate the chain of command.","create a conflict of interest."],
  "Every employee plays a role in governance by following the code of conduct and reporting problems.")
q("PD:303","After a company adopts a policy requiring board approval for any purchase over $5 million, how is management most affected?",
  ["Major decisions take more review time but face more oversight","Managers can no longer make any decisions","The company no longer needs auditors","Shareholders lose their voting rights"],
  "Governance processes add checks on management's biggest decisions, which slows them slightly but reduces risk.")

# ---------------- Communications ----------------
q("CO:017","A loan officer nods, maintains eye contact and repeats the client's main concern back in her own words. She is practicing",
  ["active listening.","passive listening.","selective listening.","interrupting."],
  "Active listening includes paying attention, showing you're engaged and paraphrasing to confirm understanding.")
q("CO:059","A client says \"I'm fine with that plan\" but crosses his arms and frowns. The advisor should",
  ["notice the mixed signal and ask what concerns he has","continue, because he said he was fine","end the meeting immediately","point out that his body language is rude"],
  "Nonverbal cues can contradict words. Asking an open question gives the client a chance to share concerns.")
q("CO:084","An advisor explaining investments to a 19-year-old first-time investor should",
  ["use simple language and everyday examples, avoiding jargon","use technical terms to show expertise","speak only about advanced strategies","give a printed prospectus and skip the explanation"],
  "Adapt communication to your audience. Plain language and examples help beginners understand.")
q("CO:061","When a judge challenges your recommendation, the best way to defend your idea objectively is to",
  ["calmly explain the facts and reasoning behind it and acknowledge valid concerns","repeat the recommendation more loudly","say the judge doesn't understand","immediately change your recommendation"],
  "Defending ideas objectively means using evidence and logic, not emotion, and staying open to good points.")
q("CO:025","Which is the best way to open a business presentation?",
  ["State the purpose and give a brief overview of what you will cover","Apologize for being nervous","Start with the details of your last point","Read the first slide word for word"],
  "A strong opening tells the audience why they should listen and where you're going.")
q("CO:086","An analyst organizes a report from the most important finding to the least important. This organization is",
  ["order of importance.","chronological order.","spatial order.","alphabetical order."],
  "Order of importance puts key information first so busy readers get it immediately.")
q("CO:087","Which graphic aid is best for showing how a company's revenue changed over the last 10 years?",
  ["Line graph","Pie chart","Organizational chart","Flowchart"],
  "Line graphs show trends over time. Pie charts show parts of a whole at one point in time.")
q("CO:091","A one-page summary at the start of a long report that gives decision makers the key findings and recommendations is a(n)",
  ["executive summary.","appendix.","bibliography.","cover letter."],
  "Executives often read only the executive summary, so it must stand on its own.")
q("CO:090","Which is a guideline for writing professional emails?",
  ["Use a clear subject line and keep the message brief and focused","Write in all capital letters for emphasis","Use emojis to sound friendly","Send sensitive client data in the body of the email"],
  "Professional emails are clear, concise and secure. Never send sensitive data unencrypted.")
q("CO:206","Which is the best practice for a financial advisor using social media?",
  ["Keep business accounts professional and follow the firm's compliance rules","Post client success stories with names and account balances","Share stock tips on a personal account","Use one account for both personal and business posts"],
  "Finance firms must follow advertising and recordkeeping rules for social media. Client information is never shared.")
q("CO:202","Compared with a phone call, a text message to a client is",
  ["fast and convenient but less suited to complex or sensitive topics","always more professional","best for delivering bad news","legally required for account changes"],
  "Digital messages are quick but lack tone of voice. Complex or sensitive conversations are better in person or by phone.")
q("CO:204","An analyst turns a spreadsheet of branch sales into a color-coded map that shows which branches are performing best. This is an example of",
  ["data visualization.","data normalization.","an audit trail.","a pro forma statement."],
  "Data visualization turns numbers into visuals such as heat maps and infographics that are easier to understand.")

# ---------------- Customer Relations ----------------
q("CR:009","A customer is angry that a check deposit is on hold. What should the employee do first?",
  ["Listen without interrupting and acknowledge the customer's frustration","Explain that it is bank policy and move on","Call security","Tell the customer to come back when calm"],
  "With a difficult customer, start by listening and showing you understand. Then explain and offer solutions.")
q("CR:007","A client asks why the bank charges a fee for paper statements. The best way to interpret this policy is to",
  ["explain the reason for the fee and offer the free e-statement option","say \"that's just the rule\"","waive every fee the client asks about","blame management for the policy"],
  "Explaining the reason behind a policy and offering alternatives helps customers accept it.")
q("CR:029","Which action best helps a new financial advisor build rapport with a client?",
  ["Remembering details the client shared, such as their children's names and goals","Talking mostly about the advisor's own achievements","Rushing through the meeting to respect the client's time","Using as much industry jargon as possible"],
  "Rapport grows from genuine interest in the client as a person.")
q("CR:030","A credit union calls members on their account anniversaries to review whether their accounts still meet their needs. The main goal is to",
  ["build and maintain long-term relationships","sell as many products as possible in one call","reduce the number of members","collect overdue payments"],
  "Regular, helpful contact builds loyalty, which keeps customers longer.")
q("CR:001","A bank advertises \"We're here when life happens\" and trains staff to help customers through big life events. This message is the bank's",
  ["brand promise.","mission statement.","privacy policy.","bylaws."],
  "A brand promise is what a company commits to deliver to customers every time.")
q("CR:019","When serving a client whose first language is not English, a bank employee should",
  ["speak clearly, avoid slang and offer translated materials if available","speak louder","avoid explaining details","ask a family member to make decisions for the client"],
  "Adapting to cultural and language differences shows respect and prevents misunderstandings.")
q("CR:017","Which use of CRM data is unethical?",
  ["Selling clients' personal information to outside marketers without permission","Reminding clients of upcoming CD maturity dates","Noting a client's preferred contact method","Tracking which services a client already uses"],
  "Ethical CRM respects privacy. Financial institutions must give privacy notices and limit sharing.")
q("CR:012","A client says, \"I don't trust advisors. You just want to sell me things.\" What is the best response?",
  ["Explain how you are paid, your duty to act in the client's best interest and how they can check your record","Promise the client guaranteed returns","Tell the client most people feel that way and move on","Offer a discount on the first product"],
  "Transparency about compensation and duties, plus tools like FINRA BrokerCheck, builds trust. Never guarantee returns.")
q("CR:012","A client's goals and risk tolerance must be understood before an advisor recommends investments. This requirement is known as",
  ["know your customer (KYC) and suitability.","front-running.","churning.","diversification."],
  "Advisors must gather client information and recommend only products that fit the client's needs.")

# ---------------- Operations ----------------
q("OP:189","Which activity is part of a bank's operations function?",
  ["Processing deposits and loan payments accurately each day","Creating a TV advertising campaign","Setting the Federal Reserve's interest rates","Writing the company's mission statement"],
  "Operations are the day-to-day activities that produce and deliver a company's products and services.")
q("OP:441","Under the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act, financial institutions must",
  ["explain their information-sharing practices to customers and protect sensitive data","guarantee every deposit up to $1 million","report all employee salaries to the public","keep all records on paper"],
  "The GLBA requires privacy notices and safeguards for customers' personal financial information.")
q("OP:064","Requiring employees to use a password plus a code sent to their phone to log in is an example of",
  ["multifactor authentication.","encryption.","a firewall.","normalization."],
  "Multifactor authentication requires two or more types of proof, making stolen passwords less useful.")
q("OP:152","An employee receives an email that looks like it's from IT asking for his password. He should",
  ["not reply and report it as a possible phishing attempt","reply with the password","forward it to coworkers","click the link to check if it's real"],
  "Phishing emails pretend to be trusted sources. Never share passwords; report suspicious messages.")
q("OP:158","A project has a defined scope, budget and deadline, and ends when the goal is reached. This describes",
  ["project management.","ongoing operations.","a fixed cost.","quality control."],
  "Projects are temporary with a specific goal. Operations are ongoing.")
q("OP:002","A bar chart showing project tasks along a timeline with their start and end dates is a",
  ["Gantt chart.","pie chart.","flowchart.","balance sheet."],
  "Gantt charts are a common project-management tool for scheduling and tracking tasks.")
q("OP:520","A project is two weeks behind schedule. The project manager should first",
  ["identify the cause of the delay and adjust the plan","cancel the project","ignore it and hope the team catches up","remove the deadline"],
  "Monitoring projects means comparing progress to the plan and taking corrective action.")
q("OP:521","Which question best evaluates whether a project succeeded?",
  ["Did it meet its goals on time and within budget?","Did everyone enjoy working on it?","Was it the most expensive project of the year?","Did it use the newest software?"],
  "Project success is measured against the original goals, schedule and budget.")
q("OP:015","Which is a main goal of the purchasing function?",
  ["Getting the right goods at the right price, quality and time","Selling products to customers","Hiring employees","Preparing tax returns"],
  "Purchasing buys the goods and services a business needs on the best terms.")
q("OP:246","A purchasing agent accepts expensive gifts from a supplier and then gives that supplier a contract. This is unethical because it",
  ["creates a conflict of interest","lowers the company's costs","follows the bid process","improves vendor performance"],
  "Gifts can influence decisions. Ethical purchasing means choosing vendors on merit.")
q("OP:161","When selecting a vendor, which factor is usually most important besides price?",
  ["Reliability and quality","How close the vendor's owner lives","The vendor's logo","How many ads the vendor runs"],
  "A cheap vendor that delivers late or poor-quality goods costs more in the end.")
q("OP:017","Which is an example of production in a service business such as a bank?",
  ["Creating and delivering a new mortgage loan for a customer","Mining raw materials","Growing crops","Building cars on an assembly line"],
  "Production is creating goods or services. For a bank, the \"product\" is its financial services.")
q("OP:019","In a company with a strong quality culture, employees",
  ["take responsibility for quality and are encouraged to report problems","leave quality to the inspection department","hide errors to avoid blame","focus only on speed"],
  "A quality culture makes quality everyone's job, supported by leadership.")
q("OP:443","All the businesses and activities involved in getting a product from raw materials to the final customer make up the",
  ["supply chain.","chain of command.","balance sheet.","value proposition."],
  "The supply chain includes suppliers, manufacturers, distributors and retailers.")
q("OP:355","A bank cuts its account-opening process from 14 steps to 6 by removing duplicate forms. This is an example of",
  ["streamlining work processes.","adding internal controls.","consolidation.","outsourcing."],
  "Streamlining removes unnecessary steps to make work faster and cheaper.")
q("OP:024","Which is an overhead (operating) cost for a tax-preparation business?",
  ["Office rent","Cost of goods sold","Owner's investment","Loan principal received"],
  "Overhead costs, like rent, utilities and insurance, are needed to run the business but aren't tied to one product or client.")

# ---------------- Economics ----------------
q("EC:001","Because a city has limited money, it must choose between building a new park and repairing roads. This illustrates",
  ["scarcity and opportunity cost.","inflation.","a monopoly.","deflation."],
  "Scarcity forces choices. The value of the option you give up is the opportunity cost.")
q("EC:003","Money, buildings and equipment used to produce goods and services are which type of economic resource?",
  ["Capital","Land","Labor","Entrepreneurship"],
  "The four factors of production are land (natural resources), labor (people), capital (tools, buildings, money) and entrepreneurship.")
q("EC:004","A bank opens a branch inside a grocery store so customers can bank where they already shop. This creates which economic utility?",
  ["Place utility","Form utility","Possession utility","Time utility"],
  "Place utility makes a product available where customers want it. Time utility is when they want it.")
q("EC:006","When prices rise because demand is high, producers are encouraged to make more. This shows the function of prices to",
  ["signal and motivate producers.","eliminate competition.","set government policy.","reduce taxes."],
  "Prices send signals: high prices tell producers to supply more, low prices tell them to supply less.")
q("EC:007","An economic system in which individuals and businesses own resources and make most decisions based on supply and demand is a",
  ["market economy.","command economy.","traditional economy.","communist economy."],
  "In a market (free enterprise) economy, private ownership and competition guide decisions.")
q("EC:009","Which is a key feature of private enterprise?",
  ["The right to own property and keep profits","Government ownership of all businesses","Fixed prices set by the government","No competition between businesses"],
  "Private enterprise includes property rights, the profit motive, competition and freedom of choice.")
q("EC:011","Which is an example of an economic business risk?",
  ["A recession reduces demand for loans","An earthquake damages a branch","An employee steals cash","A customer slips on a wet floor"],
  "Economic risks come from changes in the economy. Natural risks come from nature; human risks from people.")
q("EC:012","Several banks in a town lower fees and raise savings rates to attract customers. This is",
  ["competition.","a monopoly.","price fixing.","consolidation."],
  "Competition pushes businesses to offer better value to win customers.")
q("EC:083","How does high inflation usually affect savers who keep money in a regular savings account earning 1%?",
  ["Their money loses purchasing power","Their money gains purchasing power","Their savings are unaffected","Their interest rate automatically rises to match inflation"],
  "If inflation is higher than the interest rate earned, the real value of savings falls.")
q("EC:084","When the Federal Reserve raises interest rates, what usually happens?",
  ["Borrowing becomes more expensive and spending slows","Mortgage rates fall","Savings account rates fall","Businesses borrow more"],
  "Higher rates raise the cost of credit, cooling spending and inflation. Savers usually earn more.")
q("EC:017","The total value of all final goods and services produced in a country in one year is",
  ["gross domestic product (GDP).","the consumer price index (CPI).","the national debt.","the trade deficit."],
  "GDP measures a country's economic output. CPI measures price changes.")
q("EC:082","Which is most likely when unemployment rises sharply?",
  ["Consumer spending decreases","Consumer spending increases","Inflation rises quickly","Interest rates rise quickly"],
  "When people lose jobs, they spend less, which slows the economy.")
q("EC:100","If the U.S. dollar strengthens against the euro, what happens to U.S. companies that export to Europe?",
  ["Their products become more expensive for European buyers","Their products become cheaper for European buyers","Their products cost the same","They pay lower U.S. taxes"],
  "A stronger dollar makes U.S. goods cost more in other currencies, which can hurt exports.")
q("EC:105","Which is an external factor affecting a bank's business environment?",
  ["New federal banking regulations","The bank's employee training program","The bank's office layout","The bank's mission statement"],
  "External factors (economic, political, social, technological, legal) are outside the company's control.")

# ---------------- Information Management ----------------
q("NF:079","An analyst is researching interest-rate trends. Which source is most reliable?",
  ["The Federal Reserve's official website","An anonymous social media post","A blog with no author or date","A forum comment"],
  "Evaluate sources by authority, accuracy and date. Official government data is highly reliable.")
q("NF:078","What is the most efficient first step when searching for information online?",
  ["Use specific keywords that describe exactly what you need","Read every result on the first five pages","Search single common words","Click only on ads"],
  "Specific keywords and search operators narrow results quickly.")
q("NF:278","After analyzing data, an analyst finds that branches with longer wait times have lower customer satisfaction. What should she conclude?",
  ["There is a relationship worth investigating, but it doesn't prove wait times alone cause low satisfaction","Wait times definitely cause all dissatisfaction","The data is useless","Satisfaction causes longer wait times"],
  "Correlation suggests a relationship but does not prove cause and effect.")
q("NF:110","Why is information management important to a business?",
  ["It ensures the right information is available to the right people for decisions","It eliminates the need for employees","It guarantees higher sales","It replaces all paper records with the internet"],
  "Information management collects, stores, protects and delivers information for decision-making.")
q("NF:076","Which is a legal issue associated with information management in finance?",
  ["Protecting customers' personal financial data under privacy laws","Choosing the color of a website","Deciding the length of a meeting","Selecting office furniture"],
  "Laws such as the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act regulate how financial data is collected, shared and protected.")
q("NF:003","Which is a way technology has changed banking?",
  ["Customers can deposit checks by taking a photo with a mobile app","Customers must visit a branch for every transaction","Interest rates are now set by computers","Banks no longer need security"],
  "Mobile deposit, online banking and instant payments have changed how customers bank.")
q("NF:010","In a spreadsheet, which formula adds the values in cells B2 through B10?",
  ["=SUM(B2:B10)","=ADD(B2-B10)","=TOTAL(B2+B10)","=B2:B10"],
  "SUM with a range (B2:B10) adds every cell in that range.")
q("NF:010","A spreadsheet feature that shows only the rows meeting certain conditions, such as loans over $50,000, is",
  ["filtering.","formatting.","merging.","freezing panes."],
  "Filters hide rows that don't match the criteria so you can focus on relevant data.")
q("NF:009","In a database, each row that contains all the information about one customer is called a",
  ["record.","field.","table.","query."],
  "A record is one row (one customer). A field is one column (such as phone number).")
q("NF:139","An analyst calculates the middle value in a list of loan amounts sorted from smallest to largest. She is finding the",
  ["median.","mean.","mode.","range."],
  "The median is the middle value. It is less affected by extreme values than the mean (average).")
q("NF:148","Analyzing large amounts of data to discover hidden patterns, such as which customers are likely to close their accounts, is",
  ["data mining.","data entry.","bookkeeping.","normalization."],
  "Data mining uses software and statistics to find patterns and predict behavior.")
q("NF:013","Which is a current trend in financial services?",
  ["Using artificial intelligence to detect fraud and answer customer questions","Eliminating online banking","Returning to paper checks only","Closing all mobile apps"],
  "AI, real-time payments and digital-first banking are major current trends.")

# ---------------- Entrepreneurship, HR, Marketing, Strategic Management ----------------
q("EN:039","A person who takes on the risk of starting a new business in hopes of making a profit is a(n)",
  ["entrepreneur.","employee.","shareholder.","creditor."],
  "Entrepreneurs organize resources and accept risk to create a business.")
q("EN:040","Which is a role requirement of a small-business owner?",
  ["Making final decisions and accepting responsibility for the business's results","Working only the hours stated in a contract","Following a manager's instructions","Receiving a guaranteed salary"],
  "Owners carry the risk, make the decisions and are responsible for results.")
q("EN:044","A start-up founder tells investors her app has 50,000 users when it actually has 5,000. This is",
  ["unethical and could be fraud.","an acceptable marketing technique.","a normal part of pitching.","required by investors."],
  "Misrepresenting facts to investors is unethical and can be illegal securities fraud.")
q("EN:041","A small U.S. company that sells handmade goods online to customers in Canada and Japan is taking advantage of",
  ["international trade opportunities.","protectionism.","a trade embargo.","import quotas."],
  "E-commerce lets even small businesses reach customers around the world.")
q("EC:065","Which is a major way small businesses help a market economy?",
  ["They create jobs and introduce new ideas and competition","They eliminate the need for large companies","They set national interest rates","They prevent all inflation"],
  "Small businesses create a large share of new jobs and drive innovation.")
q("HR:410","Which activity is a main responsibility of human resources management?",
  ["Recruiting, hiring and training employees","Approving loans","Managing the company's investments","Designing advertisements"],
  "HR handles staffing, training, pay and benefits, and employee relations.")
q("HR:411","An HR manager learns that two candidates are equally qualified and chooses the one who went to her college. Why is this an ethical problem?",
  ["The decision is based on personal bias, not job-related qualifications","It is illegal to hire college graduates","HR managers cannot make hiring decisions","Both candidates must be hired"],
  "Ethical HR decisions are fair and based on job-related criteria.")
q("HR:412","A company uses software that tracks employee hours, benefits and performance reviews in one system. This is an example of",
  ["using technology in human resources management.","customer relationship management.","data mining for fraud.","project management."],
  "HR information systems (HRIS) automate payroll, benefits and records.")
q("HR:360","Which is a main purpose of new-employee orientation?",
  ["Helping new hires understand the company's policies, culture and their role","Evaluating whether to fire the employee","Setting the employee's lifetime salary","Replacing on-the-job training"],
  "Orientation helps new employees adjust quickly and become productive.")
q("MK:001","Which is the best description of marketing?",
  ["Creating, communicating and delivering value to customers","Only advertising products on TV","Manufacturing products","Keeping financial records"],
  "Marketing covers everything from understanding customers to promotion, pricing and distribution.")
q("MK:002","A bank studies which age groups use its mobile app. This is which marketing function?",
  ["Marketing-information management","Channel management","Pricing","Selling"],
  "Marketing-information management gathers and analyzes information for marketing decisions.")
q("MK:015","Which employee action best helps a bank achieve its goal of increasing customer satisfaction?",
  ["Following up with customers to make sure their problem was solved","Rushing customers to reduce wait times at any cost","Avoiding difficult customers","Recommending products the customer doesn't need"],
  "Employees contribute to company goals through everyday actions.")
q("MK:019","After a bank adds Saturday hours, new account openings rise 15%. This is an example of",
  ["a connection between a company action and its results.","an external economic factor.","a sunk cost.","a fixed budget."],
  "Businesses track how their decisions affect results to know what works.")
q("SM:001","The management function of setting goals and deciding how to achieve them is",
  ["planning.","organizing.","staffing.","controlling."],
  "Planning sets goals and strategies. Organizing arranges resources; controlling checks results against plans.")
q("SM:075","Buying insurance to cover possible losses is which risk-management strategy?",
  ["Transferring risk","Avoiding risk","Retaining risk","Ignoring risk"],
  "The four main strategies: avoid, reduce (control), transfer (insurance, contracts) and retain (accept).")
q("SM:075","A bank decides not to offer cryptocurrency trading because the risks are too high. This strategy is",
  ["avoiding risk.","transferring risk.","retaining risk.","sharing risk."],
  "Avoidance means not taking part in the risky activity at all.")
q("SM:076","When conducting a risk assessment for a company event, what should be done after identifying possible risks?",
  ["Estimate how likely each risk is and how severe its impact would be","Cancel the event","Buy insurance for every possible risk","Ignore low-cost risks entirely"],
  "Risk assessment ranks risks by likelihood and impact so resources go to the biggest threats.")
q("SM:100","Which is an external factor that can affect how a bank is managed?",
  ["Changes in interest rates set by the Federal Reserve","The bank's employee dress code","The layout of the bank's lobby","The manager's leadership style"],
  "External factors such as the economy, laws and technology shape management decisions.")
